  "notes": "Composed of {行|こう} (go) + {進|しん} (advance). Refers to organized, purposeful walking in formation. Can be used as a noun or with する as a verb ({行進|こうしん}する — to march).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {行進|こうしん}する — to march\n- {行進|こうしん}{曲|きょく} — march (music); marching song\n- {軍事|ぐんじ}{行進|こうしん} — military march\n- {平和|へいわ}{行進|こうしん} — peace march\n- {凱旋|がいせん}{行進|こうしん} — triumphal procession\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- パレード — parade (loanword; often festive or celebratory)\n- デモ{行進|こうしん} — demonstration march (protest)\n- {行列|ぎょうれつ} — procession; queue (less formal, not necessarily in formation)\n- {進軍|しんぐん} — military advance (specifically troops advancing toward battle)",
